          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "**NOAA GFS 10 m wind** at 0.5°, read live from [PacIOOS ERDDAP](https://pae-paha.pacioos.hawaii.edu/erddap/griddap/ncep_global.html): one CSV request for `u` and `v` over the next two days, 2,703 cells from 40°S to 12°N every three hours, queried with DuckDB. No tile server and no preprocessing.\n\nThe arrows and the barbs are **`vectorfield`**, a kepler.gl layer type registered by [this plugin](https://github.com/ubica-ecuador/keplergl-grafana-panel). It takes the same U/V (or speed/direction) columns as its sibling `flowfield`, so changing a layer's type between the two keeps its columns and colour ramp.\n\n- **Arrows on a screen grid**, sized and coloured by speed, over the flow field traced from the same rows. The grid is laid out in pixels, so the arrows stay legible at any zoom.\n- **Pressure and wind.** Wind streamlines over isobars coloured by how tightly they crowd, with WMO barbs on a screen grid and rain as blue dots sized by its rate. Away from the equator the wind runs nearly along the isobars; near it, it cuts across them.\n- **Airports.** The latest METAR from each airport against the nearest GFS cell. It stays on the present whatever the bar says.\n\n**The layer panel on the left of every map is live**: expand a layer to switch *Symbol* (arrow, classified arrow, wind barb) and *Placement* (screen grid, data cells); with speed and direction columns instead of u and v it also offers *Direction is* (from or towards).\n\n**The bar at the bottom of any map walks the forecast**: it opens on the step nearest to now; drag its window or press play, and both maps move together.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
